WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:11.727
Food safety puts your temperature and hygiene checks on a schedule, at every location. In this video, you’ll log a reading, deal with one out of range, and pull the inspector’s report.

2
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:22.613
Open Food safety and pick a location. Today shows every check scheduled for today, with its times: done, with the reading, due now, late, missed, or later.

3
00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:29.403
The steam table is due. Tap Log reading, type the temperature, with the safe range right above it, and save.

4
00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:33.600
The reading fills the check’s time, with your initials and when you took it.

5
00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:41.277
If a reading is out of range, Worklynq asks what you did about it, with one-tap answers like moving the food to another cooler.

6
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:49.029
Saving it opens a food safety issue ticket for the manager, at high priority, on the Operations calendar right away.

7
00:00:49.800 --> 00:01:00.744
Report is the log an inspector asks for: a table for each week, with every reading and who took it, then every problem and what was done. Print it, or save it as a PDF.

8
00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:10.984
Managers set up the checks for each location: the standard ones come with Food Code limits, or add your own, with a safe range, the times, and instructions.

9
00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:19.796
Staff can also just tell Assist: walk-in is thirty-eight. And every morning, the daily brief shows checks done, problems, and anything missed.

10
00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:28.505
That’s food safety. Next in the Features series: training. You’ll find every guide at worklynq.com/docs.

